      "content": "A rhythmic pulsing, especially when the dishwasher is supposed to be silent, sounds like something more complex than a simple leak. It's quite possible that a faulty pump or a drainage issue is causing this, even if the water isn't visibly pooling. You might want to check the circulation pump or the drain pump assembly for obstructions or internal wear. Sometimes, a tiny piece of debris can get caught in the impeller, causing it to vibrate or tap rhythmically as it tries to move water. If you can safely access the pump area, look for anything that seems out of place or loose.",
